/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Modified UNIFAC (Dortmund) group-interaction parameters -- 530 main-group pairs.

  SOURCE (the ONLY one): Gmehling, J.; Li, J.; Schiller, M., Ind. Eng. Chem. Res.
  32 (1993) 178-193, doi:10.1021/ie00013a024, Table IV, pp. 184-190 ("Modified
  UNIFAC (Dortmund) Group Interaction Parameters").  One row per printed row:
  n, m, then a_nm [K], b_nm [-], c_nm [1/K] and a_mn, b_mn, c_mn, exactly as
  the table's two column triples.  Read at the page image; the 'x 10^-e'
  exponents were classified from the printed superscripts.  `page` is the
  journal page of the row.

  EQUATION (Weidlich & Gmehling, Ind. Eng. Chem. Res. 26 (1987) 1372, eq 7;
  Gmehling et al. 1993 eq 10):
      Psi_nm = exp( -( a_nm + b_nm T + c_nm T^2 ) / T ),   T in K.

  A row's mirror (m, n) is the second triple; the diagonal is Psi = 1.  A group
  pair the paper does not print (the table holds 530 of the 990 pairs of 45
  main groups) is REFUSED by name at run time -- it is never filled from the
  original UNIFAC table or any later revision.  The paper's own flags
  ("+!", "-!", "+/-!": parameters to be revised; unreliable outside 20-125 C,
  p. 181) are NOT carried per row; the engine announces the window instead.

  LICENCE.  Only the parameters printed in this paper (and Weidlich & Gmehling
  1987) are entered; the later licensed revisions are not (DEV.md 4c C408 (c)).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

